{"id":2073,"date":"2026-08-26T00:17:28","date_gmt":"2026-08-26T00:17:28","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/?post_type=knowledgebase&#038;p=2073"},"modified":"2026-08-26T00:36:44","modified_gmt":"2026-08-26T00:36:44","slug":"opening-importing-files","status":"publish","type":"knowledgebase","link":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/db\/extra-tips\/opening-importing-files\/","title":{"rendered":"Opening &#038; Importing Files"},"content":{"rendered":"<div style=\"color: #2b2b2b; font-family: sans-serif;\">\n<h2 class=\"western\" style=\"color: #307870; margin-bottom: 10px; margin-top: 0;\">Opening &amp; Importing Files<img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignright wp-image-2084\" src=\"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/OpeningAndImportingFiles.webp\" alt=\"Opening &amp; Importing Files\" width=\"232\" height=\"173\" srcset=\"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/OpeningAndImportingFiles.webp 1388w, http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/OpeningAndImportingFiles-300x223.webp 300w, http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/OpeningAndImportingFiles-1024x763.webp 1024w, http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/OpeningAndImportingFiles-768x572.webp 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 232px) 100vw, 232px\" \/><\/h2>\n<p class=\"western\" style=\"line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 20px;\">Open Publisher is designed to act as a versatile hub for all your design assets. In addition to saving and loading its native <span style=\"font-family: 'Courier New', Courier, monospace; color: #444;\">.opub<\/span> format, the software can effortlessly open and import a wide variety of standard file types. You can bring external content into your project traditionally via the <strong>File &gt; Open<\/strong> menu, or for a faster workflow, you can simply drag &amp; drop files directly from your computer&#8217;s desktop.<\/p>\n<h3 class=\"western\" style=\"color: #307870; margin-bottom: 10px;\">Supported File Types<\/h3>\n<p><!-- Supported File Types Table (Minified) --><\/p>\n<div style=\"border: 2px solid #307870; border-radius: 16px; overflow: hidden; margin-bottom: 30px; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.05); padding: 0; background-color: #307870; line-height: 0;\">\n<table style=\"width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 0 !important; padding: 0 !important; font-size: 14px; text-align: left; border-spacing: 0; border: none; background-color: #ffffff; line-height: 1.6;\">\n<thead style=\"background-color: #307870; color: #ffffff;\">\n<tr>\n<th style=\"padding: 14px 16px; font-weight: 600; border: none;\">File Type<\/th>\n<th style=\"padding: 14px 16px; font-weight: 600; border: none;\">Extension(s)<\/th>\n<th style=\"padding: 14px 16px; font-weight: 600; border: none;\">Description<\/th>\n<\/tr>\n<\/thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"background-color: #ffffff; border-bottom: 1px solid #d9e8e6;\">\n<td style=\"padding: 12px 16px; font-weight: bold; color: #1e4d40; border-left: none; border-right: none;\">Native Format<\/td>\n<td style=\"padding: 12px 16px; font-family: 'Courier New', Courier, monospace; color: #444; border-left: none; border-right: none;\">.opub, .json<\/td>\n<td style=\"padding: 12px 16px; border-left: none; border-right: none;\">Full fidelity loading &#8211; restores your entire working session exactly as it was saved, preserving all layers, text boxes, styling, and high-resolution assets.<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr style=\"background-color: #ffffff; border-bottom: 1px solid #d9e8e6;\">\n<td style=\"padding: 12px 16px; font-weight: bold; color: #1e4d40; border-left: none; border-right: none;\">Images<\/td>\n<td style=\"padding: 12px 16px; font-family: 'Courier New', Courier, monospace; color: #444; border-left: none; border-right: none;\">.png, .jpg, .gif, .webp, etc.<\/td>\n<td style=\"padding: 12px 16px; border-left: none; border-right: none;\">Dropped or opened images are instantly placed directly onto the current page canvas as movable, resizable elements, ready to be cropped or filtered.<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr style=\"background-color: #ffffff; border-bottom: 1px solid #d9e8e6;\">\n<td style=\"padding: 12px 16px; font-weight: bold; color: #1e4d40; border-left: none; border-right: none;\">Publisher Files<\/td>\n<td style=\"padding: 12px 16px; font-family: 'Courier New', Courier, monospace; color: #444; border-left: none; border-right: none;\">.pub, .pubx<\/td>\n<td style=\"padding: 12px 16px; border-left: none; border-right: none;\">Experimental import of legacy Microsoft Publisher files. Our engine maps older assets to new formats, though layout fidelity may vary depending on the complexity of the original file.<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr style=\"background-color: #ffffff; border-bottom: 1px solid #d9e8e6;\">\n<td style=\"padding: 12px 16px; font-weight: bold; color: #1e4d40; border-left: none; border-right: none;\">Excel Spreadsheets<\/td>\n<td style=\"padding: 12px 16px; font-family: 'Courier New', Courier, monospace; color: #444; border-left: none; border-right: none;\">.xlsx, .xls<\/td>\n<td style=\"padding: 12px 16px; border-left: none; border-right: none;\">Instead of importing as raw text, spreadsheets are intelligently rendered as fully interactive, movable, and resizable table objects on the canvas, preserving your grid structure.<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr style=\"background-color: #ffffff;\">\n<td style=\"padding: 12px 16px; font-weight: bold; color: #1e4d40; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-bottom: none;\">Word Documents<\/td>\n<td style=\"padding: 12px 16px; font-family: 'Courier New', Courier, monospace; color: #444; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-bottom: none;\">.doc, .docx<\/td>\n<td style=\"padding: 12px 16px; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-bottom: none;\">Because word processors handle layouts differently than publishing software, two distinct import modes are available (see below).<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<\/div>\n<h3 class=\"western\" style=\"color: #307870; margin-bottom: 10px;\">Word Document Import Modes<img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignright wp-image-2080\" src=\"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/WordDocumentImportModes.webp\" alt=\"Word Document Import Modes\" width=\"101\" height=\"117\" srcset=\"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/WordDocumentImportModes.webp 427w, http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/WordDocumentImportModes-259x300.webp 259w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 101px) 100vw, 101px\" \/><\/h3>\n<p class=\"western\" style=\"line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 20px;\">Word processors use &#8220;flowing&#8221; text rather than absolute page coordinates. Because of this, dropping or opening a <span style=\"font-family: 'Courier New', Courier, monospace; color: #444;\">.doc<\/span> or <span style=\"font-family: 'Courier New', Courier, monospace; color: #444;\">.docx<\/span> file triggers an intelligent <strong>Import Wizard<\/strong> with two specific modes, allowing you to choose how the text is handled based on your project&#8217;s needs:<\/p>\n<p><!-- Word Import Modes Table (Minified) --><\/p>\n<div style=\"border: 2px solid #307870; border-radius: 16px; overflow: hidden; margin-bottom: 30px; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.05); padding: 0; background-color: #307870; line-height: 0;\">\n<table style=\"width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 0 !important; padding: 0 !important; font-size: 14px; text-align: left; border-spacing: 0; border: none; background-color: #ffffff; line-height: 1.6;\">\n<thead style=\"background-color: #307870; color: #ffffff;\">\n<tr>\n<th style=\"padding: 14px 16px; font-weight: 600; border: none; width: 30%;\">Import Mode<\/th>\n<th style=\"padding: 14px 16px; font-weight: 600; border: none;\">Description<\/th>\n<\/tr>\n<\/thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"background-color: #ffffff; border-bottom: 1px solid #d9e8e6;\">\n<td style=\"padding: 12px 16px; font-weight: bold; color: #1e4d40; border-left: none; border-right: none;\">Editable Text Mode<\/td>\n<td style=\"padding: 12px 16px; border-left: none; border-right: none;\">The engine extracts all paragraphs, fonts, and colours, and intelligently converts them into editable Open Publisher text boxes. This is best for articles, essays, and standard documents where you want to continue rewriting or styling the content after importing.<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr style=\"background-color: #ffffff;\">\n<td style=\"padding: 12px 16px; font-weight: bold; color: #1e4d40; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-bottom: none;\">Flattened Image Mode<br \/>\n<span style=\"font-size: 0.85em; color: #666; font-weight: normal;\">(Safe Mode)<\/span><\/td>\n<td style=\"padding: 12px 16px; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-bottom: none;\">The document is rendered as a crisp, high-resolution, uneditable background image, locking everything in place to guarantee 100% layout accuracy. Highly recommended for complex forms, technical medical tables, or any document where pixel-perfect formatting fidelity matters more than the ability to edit the text.<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Opening &amp; Importing Files Open Publisher is designed to act as a versatile hub for all your design assets. In addition to saving and loading its native .opub format, the software can effortlessly open and import a wide variety of standard file types. You can bring external content into your project traditionally via the File [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":2084,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","template":"","knowledgebase_cat":[25],"class_list":["post-2073","knowledgebase","type-knowledgebase","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","knowledgebase_cat-extra-tips"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/knowledgebase\/2073","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/knowledgebase"}],"about":[{"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/knowledgebase"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=2073"}],"version-history":[{"count":12,"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/knowledgebase\/2073\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":2090,"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/knowledgebase\/2073\/revisions\/2090"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/2084"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=2073"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"knowledgebase_cat","embeddable":true,"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/knowledgebase_cat?post=2073"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}